  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&#x2019;s and feminist funds solutions for a life free of technology-facilitated gender-based violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project objective is to promote and protect local inclusive democratic space in the digital era, through the eradication of technology-facilitated gender-based violence (TFGBV) that affects women, girls and diversities in Latin America. More specifically, this project aims to strengthen advocacy for addressing TFGBV through a targeted regional approach. The regional strategy provides added value by aligning interventions across Latin America&#x2019;s diverse legal and political landscapes. A regional focus enables the identification, comparison, and adaptation of successful laws, policies, and best practices, thereby enhancing resilience and expanding protections for Women Human Rights Defenders (WHRDs) and Women Decision Makers (WDMs) across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
